Embrace the Magic of Demons to Fight Fire with Fire

Most Demon Hunters joined Illidan on Outland as he marshaled his forces to battle the Burning Legion. You might have followed a different path, inspired by Illidan rather than directly trained by him, but the result is the same: You have embraced the magic of the Burning Legion with the singular goal of defeating it on Azeroth and every other world.

Level 1: Spellcasting
You can use an Arcane Focus (not a Druidic Focus) as a Spellcasting Focus for your Ranger spells.

Level 2: Deft Explorer
When you choose languages for the Deft Explorer class feature, choose from the language tables in chapter 2. Eredun and Nathrezim are recommended.

Level 2: Fighting Style
As a Demon Hunter, you can choose a Fighting Style feat, the Druidic Warrior option in the Player’s Handbook, or the Void Warrior option below.

Void Warrior. You learn two Warlock cantrips of your choice. Chill Touch and Mind Sliver are recommended. The chosen cantrips count as Ranger spells for you, and Wisdom is your spellcasting ability for them. Whenever you gain a Ranger level, you can replace one of these cantrips with another Warlock cantrip.

Level 3: Demon Hunter Spells
When you reach a Ranger level specified in the Demon Hunter Spells table, you thereafter always have the spell in the Spells (All) column prepared. You also have the additional spells listed in one other column of your choice.

